Richard Abraham wrote:
> 
> To List:
> 
> I hope someone can help me.
> 
> I have reached the limit of 32 terminals for network connections on
> my Tru64 4.0f machine.
> 
> I tried /dev/MAKEDEV PTYS_3.  It appeared to create 366 extra terminals
> but I still get refused when I try to log in and the original 32
> terminals are in use.

Do a sysconfig -q pts
It'll most likely say 32.
Edit your /etc/sysconfigtab and add at the bottom :

pts:
	nptys = 366


It's also described in the System conf & tuning manual. (Or was it jus
the sysadm manual...).


l8r/Jspr



