Bob Kaplow (kaplow_r@eisner.decus.org) wrote:
: Forgive me for stepping outside my VMS knowledge base and asking a Tru64Unix
: V4.0D question...
[...]

: What does this "BOOTDEVICE_PARSER: UNKNOWN PROTOCOL NAME 'SCSI'" error mean?
: What do I need to do to Tru64Unix when I move its system disk from one
: controller to another to make it bootable?

You may need to rebuild the kernel.  Some UNIX kernels can get the swap 
device name built into them and refuse to boot if you change the physical
name of the disk.  You should be able to boot the generic kernel in any
case (/genvmunix).  There should be a boot flag which allows you to
specify the disk, parition, and file name for the kernel.

