Uncle Jeff (jeffhowie@my-deja.com) wrote:
: /etc/services file. So, it's our understanding that each port should be
: reserved by the OS for only that application.

No, this understanding is wrong. Placing a port name in /etc/services
has no effect apart from giving that port a convenient symbolic name, 
which every individual program is free to use (or ignore). The only way
to actually reserve a port number is to bind() to it - in which case
it will not be available for other processes.

/Serge.P

