You can NFS-mount the disks you want to backup on the system with the
tape drive attached and run vdump on that system - works fine for our
backups.

If this is not feasible, you can do something like

vdump 0uf - /file-set | rsh remote-node 'dd of=/dev/nrmt0h bs=32k'

where /file-set is the fileset to be backed-up, and remote-node is
the system with the tape drive. There is a DSNlink article on this
(I forget if it is in the FAQ also).

John Hill
