	You really shouldn't set up a purely symmetric arrangement. Imagine if
the two machines have clocks that are 40 seconds apart. What do you want
NTP to do? Neither one will see the other as any 'better' than it, so
there will be no way to disambiguate.

	My suggestion is to think of one as the 'master' and set it to consider
its local clock at a lower stratum. Say the master fudges its local
clock to stratum 10 and slaves fudge to 11. I would use symmetric
active, both configured with local reference clocks.

	I do not recommend using prefer except in certain specific instances
(like with the ATOM reference driver). I think using the stratum setting
is easier.

	DS

