	Not a typo -- someone left "quoted printable" encoding enabled[1],
whereby non-ASCII (i.e. 8-bit) characters are translated to "=XX" where XX
is the hexadecimal code for the byte.  Naturally, this makes real "="
characters ambiguous, so they have to be translated too, into "=3D".

[1] Or perhaps, even worse, deliberately turned it on[2]!
