We think we have finally found the elusive "quota underflow" bug in
AdvFS.  About 2 weeks ago we found a way to reproduce the problem (a
reproducable bug is always easier to fix :-), and last week one of the
engineers tracked down and fixed the root cause of the quota underflow
errors.

This fix has been put into all the current development source pools and
the fix is being backported to the different support pools.

This fix should eventually make it into the Tru64 UNIX patch kits and
should be included as part of the v4.0g and v5.0a releases.  I don't
know how long it will take to make it into a patch kit, but I would
expect it to take a little while to get through the patch kit release
process.

Once the fix is available, it is recommended that quotacheck be run
after the fix is installed to clean up any residual quota inaccuracies,
and hopefully from that point forward quota underflow will be history.

Until then, the work around is to run quotacheck to correct the quota
information.



