Albert Chin (china@my-the-written-word.com) wrote:
: I'm running DU4.0D on an AS 200 and am running into the following:
:   halted CPU 0
: 
:   halt code = 7
:   machine check while in PAL mode
:   PC = 14020
: 
: What does 'halt code = 7' indicate?

Halt code 7 means "machine check while in PAL mode".  

On very old machines, there was not enough room in the ROMs that contained the
console software to store messages, so the consoles would just say "halt
code=7".  Then, you'd have to look up in a book what it meant. 

Current systems now have enough room to store the messages, so they can also
print them out, but the console code spec requires that the code number still
be printed.

        Stu



