Please read your USER MANUAL CAREFULLY.

COM port 1, or the so-called Console Port on the AlphaServer systems has
been specially engineered to do unique things. The requisite settings to be
made by you in the SRM are covered in the User Manual.

In addition, many AlphaServer in fact have 3 serial ports, one of which is
really special and is referred to as the RCM, Remote Console Management
port. Again, this is described in excruciating detail in the User Manual.

If you are using Windows NT on an AlphaServer, then there is a specific
jumper to be set on a circuit card inside the system to make it more
compatible with Windows NT.


rtt



