"Mark Orndorff" <maorndorff@yahoo.com> wrote:
> New to True64. I 've heard good and bad about AdvFS. I want to go with a
> logged file system. Any reasons to avoid AdvFsS?

I keep hearing rumors that ADVFS is subject to corruption, and there are
bugs that do seem to keep cropping up.  UFS has been around for, what, 15
years now?  It's probably about as bullet-proof and well debugged as any
file system code ever can be.

But, ADVFS offers wonderful advantages in being able to dynamically
partition disks and re-arrange physical storage capacity as needs change. 
We've been running ADVFS on our production machines for a couple years
now, and at this point, I don't know how I ever survived without it.



