> Does anyone know hot to contorl (espcecially) NumLock key?  I need to have
> console NumLock key automatically set to active when the system is booted.
> 
> I hope this is very simple on DIGITAL UNIX.

The `xset' utility maintains the leds.

The `dxkeycaps' utility can be used to programmatically simulate key
press and key release events (this may be a bit tricky, but it appears
that it might be able to do this).

If `xdpyinfo' shows that you are using the XKB extension, you may find
some utility in the XKB functions:

man -k XKB
dxkbledpanel (1X)       - Present an on-screen display of keyboard indicators.
xkbcomp (1X)            - compile XKB keyboard description
xkbdfltmap (1X)         - Determine default X keymap for locale and keyboard
xkbprint (1X)           - print an XKB keyboard description


If all of these routes fail, it may be possible to write a short X
program that does what you want.  It will have to generate synthetic X
events (which your X server may or may not decide to ignore for
security purposes).


Mind you, it has been a few years since I did any X window programming.  I
got most of this information from using `man' on my Tru64 Unix 5.0 system.


Good luck!

