the only bugs i have seen were the assumptions compaq likes to put for
defaults.

if advfs runs into a bad bitmap or corrupted table it doesnt try to fix
it.  you have to patch the kernel so advfs can fix it on the fly instead
of having your system panic because of advfs.

the other bug was never explained...  i had every advfs guru, kernel
guru, and unix guru on the east coast looking at my system panic at whim
because of advfs... then it just went away without a trace...  doesnt
make me feel good when that happens!

the latest patch kits fixes alot of advfs problems.  i just havent ran
across half of them yet.

like i said before, dunix 5 fixes alot of things and introduces new
features.  DEC urr COMPAQ was re-assuring me of that at our COMPAQ sales
visit to DEC to meet the engineers.

