I agree: it is never a good idea to work as root for "normal" usage.

So try this:

1. Set all gettys but console to "off" in /etc/inittab.

2. Make sure that none of the remote login daemons is started, or make
them unavailable (telnetd, rlogind, etc.)
You can use the TCP-Wrapper (which is avail. in the Public Domain,
e.g. on a Linux-Distribution) to do "fine tuning".

3. You might also want to install the Enhanced Security package.


