Organization: Massachvsetts Institvte of Technology
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

In article <37F5694E.77300844@cco.caltech.edu>,
Arthur J. Chirino <art01@cco.caltech.edu> wrote:

>Should I simply edit s00inet and replace tu0 with tu1 or is something
>insidious going on in TRU64 5.0? Does anyone know why tu1 instead of tu0
>is found if the 4d60t driver is in place? Thank you very much in
>advance.

Like Solaris, Tru64 5.0 has a persistent map of device IDs to device
names (device ID could be "the occupant of slot 9" or "the disk with
serial number 42").  Unlike Solaris, the map isn't human-readable.
Moving a card may cause it to be renamed.  The new ID should not
change again so replacing tu0 with tu1 is the right solution.

-- 
    John Carr (jfc@mit.edu)



