this is a RAID pedestal?  "re" devices are usually SWXCR/KZPSC based
internal RAID controllers. so there must be a few BA35x cabs hanging off
it...

your output looks like you're using UFS.  so you are pretty much stuck!
AdvFS will allow you to expand volumes on the fly (except root).  you might
have to use LSM to bind some volumes together to get more space.  but that
requires a license (NET-SUPP-xxx or LSM-xx).

if you have the latest firmware for the SWXCR/KZPSC-AC you can bind 2 RAID
sets together...  i can't remember exactly which model does that.

you're correct in your calculation to figure out GB from 1024K bytes.  so
you have roughly 1.5 GB free on the partition.

