HxMan wrote:
> 
> There are two disk drives in my Dec box, and only one is mounted. How
> do I go about mounting the second?
> 
> Thanks Me

Assuming Digital UNIX 4.0e and lower.

Well, if you know the device ID/name (SCSI number), and the device
special files exist (in /dev), you will need to disklabel the drive,
newfs it, and mount it. If you want to have it mounted everytime the
system boots, an entry for the drive will need to be placed in the
/etc/fstab file. 

man MAKEDEV
man disklabel
man newfs
man mount
man fstab

There are also the GUI tools to do it from CDE, and alternate file
systems. Everything is described in the DUNIX manuals:

http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/pub_page/doc_list.html
http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V40D_HTML/APS2RETE/DOCU_012.HTM#BLOCK205

