> 
> What is the name of the GUI tool?????? Can I just start that specific
> tool on my desktop???

I think it is called diskconfig. It needs to be run as root.

If you are running the CDE desktop, go into your Application Manager (on
toolbar as file cabinet drawer with calculator/ruler/pencil sticking
up). Once there, you want "System_Admin", "Configuration", then "Disk".

IIRC, diskconfig can only deal with devices that already have a device
special file in /dev. Which means you might still need to do a MAKEDEV
for your device.

If all else fails, use the "standard" ways. Using MAKEDEV, disklabel,
newfs, and the rest are not that hard once you get used to it. They are
described in the DUNIX manuals, and O'Reilly's "System Administration
Essentials" book.

