Strange problem since it works with other machines...

Any error messages in /var/adm/messages ?

Something like CRC errors or other network related errors.
Try grep'ing on tu0, fta0 (or what type of NIC you have) in messages.

If you run with ethernet cards, then lock them to the speed you're
running at. This is done in the boot-prompt.
Type "show ewa*" to see the current setting (ewa = ethernet cards like
DE500). 
It's the ewaX_mode parameter, where X is the NIC number (0 if you only
have one NIC).
This is Auto by default, with works, but not good. Lock it to FastFD if
you're running 100MBit/s switched and so forth.
Remember to do the same on your switch. 
This will improve performance and prevent errors.

If it still doesn't work and you still get errors, try with other cables
or other hub/switch ports.

BTW: As far as I remember 4.0b is not Y2K compliant. You need 4.0d patch
3.



