This is precisely the problem I saw when I upgraded from Digital UNIX
V4.0b to V4.0d (the Solaris machine is running 2.5.1, but this is not
directly relevant). It appears that something has changed in rmt to make
this combination no longer work.
I used to do

ufsdump 0uf <du_node>:/dev/nrmt0h /dev/rdsk/c0t0d0s0

where <du_node> is my Digital UNIX node.

Now I find that something like

ufsdump 0uf - /dev/rdsk/c0t0d0s0 | rsh <du_node> 'dd of=/dev/nrmt0h
bs=32k'

is necessary. There is a DSNLINK article discussing remote backup where I

found the above magic.
I HAVE tried to recover such a backup - I found recovery of a complete
dump
is OK, but trying to use interactive mode to select individual files does
not work.

Regards,
John Hill

