Mark Holloway <mholloway@flashmail.com> wrote:
: Can anyone tell me which file needs to be modified to bump up the refresh
: rates on Digital Unix 4.0F?  I'm using a Permedia II based video card and I
: know it supports 85 and 100hz.  I believe the default is 72hz and it's
: killing me on the 21" monitor!

Add command line options to the Xdec command line.  The typicalplace is in
/usr/var/X11/Xserver.conf, the canonical location of the
server configuration file on DU.  Options:

        -screen[<num>] <width>[x<height>]
        -vsync[<num>] <rate>
        -I -e3stereo[<num>] <rate>

Where:

        <num>        Screen number starting from 0
        <width>      Width in pixels
        <height>     Height in pixels
        <rate>       Refresh rate in Hz

-screen and -vsync must be before any -I option and -e3stereo
applies only to 4D40T-4D60T cards.  Examples:

        -screen0 1920x1280
        -vsync 75 -screen 1280

See also the X, Xdec, Xserver.conf manual, and the
/usr/var/X11/Xservers file.

Mihaly




