On Thu, 30 Sep 1999, Mapu wrote:

> Someone or something chowned almost everything on my DEC Alpha system
> running Digital Unix to an unpriviledged user yesterday. I seem to have
> pretty much recovered from it, except when trying to start my secure web
> servers, I get a "No more ptys..contact your system administrator" error
> message. Previous to this incident, there was no problem. I'm looking for
> info on how to fix this so that the processes will start. Any ideas?
> 
> Thanks for any help in advance...
> 

xterm on Digital Unix produces the same error message if started
without root privileges, which happens when the SUID root bit is
missing. Since chown has the side effect of removing the SUID bits,
I would guess that a SUID bit is missing on one of your binaries.

Timo

