In article <jIgJ3.1821$Lg2.85283@news2.bora.net>, HongSub, Shin
<shinhs@e-net.co.kr> writes
>Now I use "Tru64 Unix". When I login system as "root", there is no problem.
>The problem is arised when normal users login system like this.
>
>    Tru64 Unix...
>
>    login: auser
>    password: ******
>    Too many users logged on already
>    Try again later
>
>There is no any users except for "root" and "auser" in this system.
>How can I correct this problem?...
>Please tell me...

You have the OSF-BASE licence installed, which only allows root access
from the console. To allow normal users to access the machine, you also
need to install an OSF-USR licence - this will either allow a specified
number of users to connect at any one time, or be for unlimited use.

If this machine is new, you may have a OSF-USR licence PAK somewhere in
your paperwork, and quite possibly a Server Extensions (OSF-SVR) too.

Chris
